WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.852
Adobe Creative Cloud is useful in eLearning as a media and asset-production ecosystem.

2
00:00:05.852 --> 00:00:16.606
It can support the creation of visuals, audio, video, motion, documents, branding elements, and reusable design assets that eventually become part of a course.

3
00:00:16.606 --> 00:00:22.537
It is not, by itself, a learning management system or a complete instructional strategy.

4
00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:28.863
It is a toolkit that helps production teams make learning materials clearer and more polished.

5
00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:32.896
A healthy eLearning workflow separates responsibilities.

6
00:00:32.896 --> 00:00:36.217
Authoring tools assemble the course experience.

7
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:41.278
Media production tools create graphics, narration, video, and documents.

8
00:00:41.278 --> 00:00:44.678
Review workflows collect comments and approvals.

9
00:00:44.678 --> 00:00:47.920
SCORM packages package the course for tracking.

10
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.167
LMS platforms launch the course, manage learner access, and report completion or score data.

11
00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:59.544
Confusing these roles can lead to unrealistic expectations and messy projects.

12
00:00:59.544 --> 00:01:12.275
Creative Cloud assets can include diagrams, icons, screen graphics, course thumbnails, narration audio, short videos, motion graphics, PDFs, job aids, worksheets, and visual summaries.

13
00:01:12.275 --> 00:01:20.815
These assets may be used inside a SCORM course, a knowledge base, a blended learning program, or a performance-support library.

14
00:01:20.815 --> 00:01:27.221
The same source asset might also be exported in different formats for different delivery needs.

15
00:01:27.221 --> 00:01:31.332
Instructional design should come before visual production.

16
00:01:31.332 --> 00:01:41.059
Before opening a design or editing tool, the team should know the learning goal, audience, task context, content scope, and assessment approach.

17
00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:46.436
Without that plan, production can drift toward attractive but unfocused media.

18
00:01:46.436 --> 00:01:53.869
The best visuals and audio support a learning outcome; they do not compensate for a course that lacks structure.

19
00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:57.427
Use Creative Cloud to clarify, focus, and reinforce.

20
00:01:57.427 --> 00:01:59.958
A diagram can explain a relationship.

21
00:01:59.958 --> 00:02:03.121
A short video can demonstrate motion or timing.

22
00:02:03.121 --> 00:02:06.838
A job aid can help learners after the course is complete.

23
00:02:06.838 --> 00:02:08.656
The goal is not decoration.

24
00:02:08.656 --> 00:02:16.643
The goal is to create assets that help learners understand, complete, apply, and revisit the material when they need it.
